{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "about": "Worker adapters (F3): one entry per coding CLI, every CLI-specific name in data. Item P owns id, binary, token_env, model_flags, config_files, tools (DC-12: tool name -> read|write|shell|other and the input pointers of its path or command) and policy (target file and owned pointers, one config shape list per policy rule kind, a hook where the CLI runs one, fixed entries, what could not be verified). In a template {name}, {home}, {tail}, {path}, {word}, {sub}, {command}, {binary}, {pattern} are the rule's items, {stack} the stack folder; the secret_read sets are name (every file name glob), prefix (a name glob that starts a word), suffix (a *-glob whose literal end ends a word, so *.key is not .keys()), home, tail (a home glob's last two parts, as the rule's text patterns name it), file (file_deny: for a read config only) and allow (allow and file_allow). Item A owns the rest; the schema describes each field.",
  "run_env": {
    "adapter": "STELLA_ADAPTER",
    "capabilities_url": "STELLA_CAPABILITIES_URL"
  },
  "env_keep": [
    "PATH",
    "HOME",
    "USER",
    "LOGNAME",
    "SHELL",
    "LANG",
    "LC_ALL",
    "LC_CTYPE",
    "TERM",
    "TZ",
    "TMPDIR",
    "NO_PROXY",
    "no_proxy",
    "HTTP_PROXY",
    "HTTPS_PROXY",
    "http_proxy",
    "https_proxy"
  ],
  "output_cap": 4000,
  "stop_grace_s": 10,
  "read_cap_bytes": 1048576,
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "opencode",
      "label": "OpenCode",
      "status": "active",
      "binary": "opencode",
      "token_env": "STELLA_RUN_TOKEN",
      "tools": {
        "read": {
          "class": "read",
          "path": "/path"
        },
        "edit": {
          "class": "write",
          "path": "/path"
        },
        "write": {
          "class": "write",
          "path": "/path"
        },
        "grep": {
          "class": "read",
          "path": "/path"
        },
        "glob": {
          "class": "read",
          "path": "/pattern"
        },
        "list": {
          "class": "read",
          "path": "/path"
        },
        "bash": {
          "class": "shell",
          "command": "/command"
        },
        "webfetch": {
          "class": "other"
        },
        "task": {
          "class": "other"
        },
        "shell": {
          "class": "shell",
          "command": "/command"
        },
        "skill": {
          "class": "other"
        }
      },
      "config_files": [
        "opencode.json",
        "opencode.jsonc",
        ".opencode"
      ],
      "model_flags": {
        "names": [
          "opencode",
          "@opencode/cli"
        ],
        "model": "--model",
        "fallback": "-m",
        "mode": "--agent",
        "mode_forbidden": [],
        "skip": [],
        "run": [
          "run"
        ],
        "no_model": [
          "run",
          "mini",
          "acp",
          "serve",
          "api",
          "--version",
          "-v",
          "--help",
          "-h",
          "upgrade",
          "update",
          "uninstall",
          "debug",
          "auth",
          "mcp",
          "plugin",
          "models",
          "stats",
          "session",
          "service",
          "reload",
          "pair"
        ],
        "model_prefix": "",
        "deny_patterns": [
          "*--model *",
          "*--model=*",
          "*-m *"
        ]
      },
      "policy": {
        "target": {
          "file": "opencode.json",
          "owned_pointers": [
            "/permission/bash",
            "/permission/edit",
            "/permission/read",
            "/permission/external_directory"
          ]
        },
        "worktree_ref": null,
        "fixed": [
          {
            "pointer": "/permission/bash",
            "key": "bin/escalate.sh *",
            "value": "allow"
          },
          {
            "pointer": "/permission/bash",
            "key": "{stack}/bin/escalate.sh *",
            "value": "allow"
          }
        ],
        "shapes": {
          "model_limits": [
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/bash",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "forbidden": [
                  "{binary} {pattern}",
                  "* {binary} {pattern}",
                  "*/{binary} {pattern}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "protected_read": [
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/bash",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "owner": [
                  "*{name}*"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/edit",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "owner": [
                  "*{name}*"
                ],
                "repo": [
                  "{path}",
                  "{path}/*"
                ],
                "home": [
                  "~/{home}/*"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/read",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "owner": [
                  "*{name}*"
                ],
                "repo": [
                  "{path}",
                  "{path}/*"
                ],
                "home": [
                  "~/{home}/*"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "secret_read": [
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/bash",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "prefix": [
                  "*/{name}*",
                  "* {name}*"
                ],
                "suffix": [
                  "*{name}",
                  "*{name} *",
                  "*{name}'*",
                  "*{name}\"*",
                  "*{name};*",
                  "*{name}|*",
                  "*{name})*",
                  "*{name}>*",
                  "*{name}&*"
                ],
                "home": [
                  "*/{home}*",
                  "*~/{home}*"
                ],
                "tail": [
                  "*{tail}*"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/read",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "name": [
                  "{name}",
                  "*/{name}"
                ],
                "home": [
                  "*/{home}",
                  "*/{home}/*"
                ],
                "file": [
                  "{name}",
                  "*/{name}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/read",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "allow",
              "templates": {
                "allow": [
                  "{name}",
                  "*/{name}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "commit_rule": [
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/bash",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "global": [
                  "git {word} *",
                  "git {word}=*"
                ],
                "sub": [
                  "git {word}",
                  "git {word} *",
                  "git * {word} *"
                ],
                "option": [
                  "git *{word}*"
                ],
                "sub_args": [
                  "git {sub} {word}",
                  "git {sub} {word} *",
                  "git {sub} * {word}",
                  "git {sub} * {word} *"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "dispatcher_only": [
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/bash",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "command": [
                  "{command}",
                  "{command} *"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "write_boundary": [
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/external_directory",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "outside": [
                  "*"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/external_directory",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "allow",
              "templates": {
                "writable": [
                  "{path}",
                  "{path}/*"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/edit",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "config": [
                  "{name}",
                  "{name}/*",
                  "*/{name}",
                  "*/{name}/*"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "pointer": "/permission/bash",
              "form": "map",
              "value": "deny",
              "templates": {
                "config": [
                  "*{name}*"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "unverified": [
          "pattern semantics (absolute or project-relative paths, * across /, which of two matching patterns wins) are taken from the patterns the repo config already used and the CLI binary's strings; opencode.ai is not on the firewall allowlist",
          "external_directory gates every tool call (read, edit, write, list, grep, glob, bash) that names a path outside the project folder, not only writes; it is rendered from the write_boundary rule as deny for every path but the run's worktree and run tmp, so a read outside them (the stack's docs, a parent card's worktree) is denied too: the write boundary is stricter here than on the hook CLI",
          "the tool input names (filePath, path, command) come from the CLI binary's strings",
          "whether a ~/ pattern is expanded to the home folder (the protected home folders are written ~/<folder>/* so a project's own .claude or .hermes folder is not hit)",
          "model_flags are read from `opencode --help` and `opencode run --help` (v2.0.26): --model (and its short form -m, kept in fallback since the CLI has no fallback flag), --agent (an agent of the config may name a model; no value is forbidden), no flag that skips permissions (--auto approves only what is not denied). Every subcommand is in no_model because a run without --model uses the configured default, which container-start pins to the resolver's worker link; the model guard then judges only an explicit --model or -m. @opencode/cli is the npm package name (npx form)",
          "config_files: OpenCode reads a project opencode.json, opencode.jsonc and .opencode/ (from the working folder up to the git root) above the OPENCODE_CONFIG file (OpenCode config docs, not run here), so the write_boundary rule denies writing them anywhere in the worktree (RT3-07)"
        ]
      },
      "version_cmd": [
